rem ACMP 191 - Smooth Numbers (Гладкие числа)
rem Solved in Euler 1-15 style with array-oriented combinatorial ranking.
rem
rem A smooth number has decimal digits in non-decreasing order:
rem   1 <= d_1 <= d_2 <= ... <= d_L <= 9 (digits cannot contain 0).
rem For length L, the number of such sequences is C(L + 8, 8).
rem We find length L via vector scan + boolean count, then determine each digit
rem position-by-position using prefix sums of combination counts without nested loops.

use io
use cli
use numbers
use sequences

arg N integer = 239

rem Cumulative count of smooth numbers of each length up to 70
Lengths = 1 to 70
Counts = (Lengths + 8) binomial 8
PrefixCounts = Counts scan + with 0 array

L = (PrefixCounts less N) count
RemN = N - (PrefixCounts (L - 1))

AnswerText = ""
D = 1

for Pos in 1 to L
  RemLen = L - Pos
  Candidates = D to 9
  Ways = (RemLen + 9 - Candidates) binomial RemLen
  CumWays = Ways scan + with 0 array
  Skip = (CumWays less RemN) count
  Chosen = Candidates (Skip - 1)
  AnswerText = AnswerText + (Chosen text)
  RemN = RemN - (CumWays (Skip - 1))
  D = Chosen
end

Answer = AnswerText integer
Answer print
